{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/207624?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/207624?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/207624?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/207624?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/207624?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/207624?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A207624"}, "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Ingelman, G."}, {"full_name": "Schlein, P.E."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "152", "page_end": "260", "year": 1985, "page_start": "256", "journal_title": "Phys.Lett.B"}], "texkeys": ["Ingelman:1984ns"], "imprints": [{"date": "1985"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "We suggest that high- p t jets may emerge from diffractively produced high mass states. Experimental measurements of such high- p t structure would give new valuable insight about the nature of the exchanged pomeron, or pomeron-like object. With the assumption of an effective gluon distribution for the pomeron structure, we estimate the cross section for the process p \u0304 + p \u2192 p \u0304 +X , where X contains two high- p t jets. Observable rates are found at SPS and Fermilab collider energies."}], "control_number": 207624, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0370-2693(85)91181-5"}], "titles": [{"title": "Jet Structure in High Mass Diffractive Scattering"}], "author_count": 2, "document_type": ["article"]}, "updated": "2023-03-07T02:14:23.083786+00:00", "id": "207624", "created": "1984-11-01T00:00:00+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Lett.B%2C152%2C256&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publication_info,arxiv_eprints.value,dois.value,texkeys,abstracts.value,document_type,imprints,isbns,collaborations